-# FAA AWA-619 and the two 09:24 entries
+# FAA Box 23 fax and event-log records
 
-November 5, 2026 · B129 / PD01 source check · Public derivative of the separately preserved source study
+November 8, 2026 Eastern. B129 / PD01 / PD07. Three one-page FAA records were retrieved through the National Archives catalog. The **fax log** records a September 20 received transmission with a page error. The **incident/event sheet** concerns a November 13 screening incident. The cataloged **report of September 11 activities** is a list of questions for preparing a report. Each record advances identification of a source previously known by title or locator. [National Archives finding aid, Box 23](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid-12-23)
 
-This study follows the public correction's source trail from [the prior ADA-30 comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/f425336303bbad671cb6943ff69941d4148b1aeb/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-ada30-layout-2026-11-05/README.md) to four National Archives copies of the FAA's *Chronology of events on 9-11-01*, catalogued under AWA-619. These copies contain a NEADS attribution that was missing from the scoped 09:24 rows of the previously reviewed FAA operations fax. No source examined identifies AWA-619 as the native computerized event log.
+| Item | Exact observations and scope |
+| --- | --- |
+| **DCC-910**, physical p. 1, upper heading and result table | The finding aid description reads `Fas Log Report`. The catalog object name uses `FAX log report`. The page header reads `Fax Log Report` and `Sep-20-01 01:15 PM`. The one visible row has `Error on page 1`, Pages `01`, Type `Received`, Date `Sep-20`, Time `01:14P` and Duration `00:00:42`. The masked fields remain excluded. [Catalog item](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34914763) |
+| **DCC-917**, physical p. 1, fax header and form heading | The header reads `NOV. 13. 2001 4:08PM` and is addressed to `ATCSCC`. The form reads `INCIDENT/EVENT LOG SHEET`, Date `11/13/01`, Time `1414` and identifies a TACA Airlines gate-screening incident. The form and fax clocks are distinct. The date glyphs in the OCR are garbled. [Catalog item](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34914771) |
+| **DCC-929**, physical p. 1, heading and embedded lines 4–17 | The heading begins `Items for a report`. On the date, the image appears to show printed `9/1/01` with a pen mark across the day and handwritten `11` above it. The embedded date fragment reads `9/r10 1`. The page asks about initial notification, call-up inclusion, whom the Command Center notified and by what method, and air traffic cell activation. Preserve the mark and printed and extracted readings separately. The document supplies questions and leaves the answers open. [Catalog item](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7603156) |
 
-## Preserve the 09:24 entries and their different attributions
+The recovered DCC-917 body resolves the previous **access** gap for that item. The earlier attempt saved an HTTP 200 HTML body from a different catalog-media URL. The current catalog returned a linked one-page PDF. Its date, form and subject identify it as a separate event from the September 11 ACC log sought here. This says nothing about whether another event sheet or computer export survives. [Prior DCC-917 access observation](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/57d7c8b17fb83a8ad089850aae49e8c3cb22469e/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-acc-event-chronology-comparison-2026-11-05/README.md)
 
